                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Esther 8:2",
        "book": "Esther",
        "chapter": 8,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And Esther spake yet again before the king, and fell down at his feet, and besought him with tears to put away the mischief of Haman the Agagite, and his device that he had devised against the Jews.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 154,
            "end": 160,
            "text": "Esth. 3:9 (8–11)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Esther 8:3",
        "book": "Esther",
        "chapter": 8,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Then the king held out the golden sceptre toward Esther. So Esther arose, and stood before the king,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "Esth. 4:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Esth. 4:11.",
            "prettyString": "Esther 4:11",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "esther",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 4,
                    "end": 4,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 11,
                        "end": 11
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Esther 8:4",
        "book": "Esther",
        "chapter": 8,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And said, If it please the king, and if I have found favour in his sight, and the thing seem right before the king, and I be pleasing in his eyes, let it be written to reverse the letters devised by Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, which he wrote to destroy the Jews which are in all the king’s provinces:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 92
          },
          {
            "start": 122,
            "end": 124
          },
          {
            "start": 281,
            "end": 284
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Esther 8:5",
        "book": "Esther",
        "chapter": 8,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "For how can I endure to see the evil that shall come unto my people? or how can I endure to see the destruction of my kindred?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Esther 8:6",
        "book": "Esther",
        "chapter": 8,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Then the king Ahasuerus said unto Esther the queen and to Mordecai the Jew, Behold, I have given Esther the house of Haman, and him they have hanged upon the gallows, because he laid his hand upon the Jews.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Esther 8:7",
        "book": "Esther",
        "chapter": 8,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Write ye also for the Jews, as it liketh you, in the king’s name, and seal it with the king’s ring: for the writing which is written in the king’s name, and sealed with the king’s ring, may no man reverse.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 197,
            "end": 204,
            "text": "Esth. 1:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Esth. 1:19.",
            "prettyString": "Esther 1:19",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "esther",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 19,
                        "end": 19
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Esther 8:8",
        "book": "Esther",
        "chapter": 8,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Then were the king’s scribes called at that time in the third month, that is, the month Sivan, on the three and twentieth day thereof; and it was written according to all that Mordecai commanded unto the Jews, and to the lieutenants, and the deputies and rulers of the provinces which are from India unto Ethiopia, an hundred twenty and seven provinces, unto every province according to the writing thereof, and unto every people after their language, and to the Jews according to their writing, and according to their language.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 519,
            "end": 527,
            "text": "Esth. 1:22."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 77
          },
          {
            "start": 122,
            "end": 125
          },
          {
            "start": 285,
